  "description": "MAINTAINER RULING #984, Q1, the same-tick half: `once per occurrence` counts occurrences, not ticks. Two deliveries of `acme.shake` land on the SAME tick 1, and the single registered handler fires twice within that tick -- exactly as `on_key` already fired twice for a key pressed twice (`on-key-repeated-press-fires-twice`), which is the sibling asymmetry the ruling removed. This is a different code path from the across-tick fixture beside it: there, two separate drains each find one pending occurrence; here, ONE drain must preserve the multiplicity of its pending queue rather than collapsing it to a set. An implementation that de-duplicates same-tick occurrences prints once and passes the across-tick fixture, so both are needed.",
